\author{Compiled by Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5) for Andr\'as Kornai}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Beeke (ISO 639-3 bkf) is a Bantu (Atlantic-Congo) language of the Democratic Republic of the Congo, spoken in Ituri along the Mambasa--Kisangani road. Its classification is uncertain; it may be a divergent form of Bali. Estimates put speakers at under about 1,000, and Endangered Languages notes it is giving way to Ndaka. Joshua Project reports no Bible translation or Jesus Film for it. No educational materials were found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia (stub) on the Beeke language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beeke_language}
\item Glottolog family tree page for Beeke: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/beek1238.bigmap.html}
\item Endangered Languages Project entry: \url{https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/584}
\item Verbix endangered-languages page: \url{https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Beeke}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project people-group profile (population about 2,600--2,700, ethnic group): \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/10760}
\item Joshua Project language page: \url{https://www.joshuaproject.net/index.php/languages/bkf}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None found.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Very little exists for Beeke. Any curriculum would require basic documentation first, and given the shift toward Ndaka, neighbouring-language resources may matter, but none were searched here.
\end{document}
